schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: "USDC's March 2023 depeg to ~$0.87 (Silicon Valley Bank exposure)"
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    In March 2023, USDC briefly fell to about $0.87 because Circle had $3.3
    billion of its reserves stuck in Silicon Valley Bank when that bank
    failed; it recovered fully within days once the money was secured.
  evidence: >-
    Article cites a CoinDesk report ("Circle confirms $3.3B stuck at
    Silicon Valley Bank") in its References section.
  source_lineage: src/content/docs/stablecoins.md
  interpretation: >-
    Used as the article's central "real breaks happen" example, to
    counterbalance the reassurance that fiat-backed stablecoins are safe —
    even a fully-reserved, regularly-audited coin depegged under real
    counterparty risk.
  uncertainty: >-
    Matches the well-documented March 2023 SVB/USDC depeg event; not
    independently re-verified against the cited CoinDesk article in this
    ingestion pass.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/stablecoins.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
